{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>To all of them he gave changes of garment.</b> The lamed has a patach." "<b>Changes of garment.</b> Tunics and trousers, which people normally change. Similar to it is ״שמלתו לעורו״ (his garment for his skin) — this is the tunic adjacent to his skin. And one says: garments of clothing, because he caused them to tear their garments unjustly when he ordered the goblet placed in Binyamin's pack, and they were embarrassed that their garments were torn. And to Binyamin, since he was not involved in his sale, he gave three hundred silver. But to the rest of his brothers who sold him, he did not give, in order to penalize each one ten hands more than the price of a slave. As our Sages said in Gittin, chapter HaSholei'ach: one who sells his slave to an idolater — they penalize him up to ten times his value. And the three hundred silver are ten times the price of a slave, as it is written in Parashat Mishpatim: ״כסף שלשים שקלים יתן לאדוניו״ (thirty shekels of silver he shall give to his master)." "<b>And five changes of garment.</b> One for tearing his garment with his brothers; a second because he is his maternal brother; a third for the shame he brought upon him by putting the name of theft on him; and two for which he was liable to pay double restitution. Another interpretation: <b>and five changes of garment</b> — in the manner of ״ותרב משאת בנימן ממשאת כלם״ — five times."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:43.844731041Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}